data/_fetched/
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# NOT results/ -- it was here, copied from a misreading of the scaffold rule. That rule says
# never COPY a result between kits (a result belongs to the run that produced it); it does not
# say do not commit one. docs-qa tracks its results, every published figure names the run file
# it came from, and the register gate checks that a record's source exists in the kit. An
# uncommitted result is evidence nothing can cite.
# ⚠︎ A GLOB, NOT A NAME. This read `gold.jsonl` until 2026-08-09, and the unseen-schema probe
# writes `gold-banks_2.jsonl` — which `git status` duly offered to commit. The whole
# fetch-never-vendor design of this kit exists so no CC BY-SA utterance is redistributed here, and
# a literal filename defeated it the first time a second corpus existed. Caught by checking before
# the commit, not by the rule.
gold*.jsonl
